#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:3
msgid "Fast Snapshot Load"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:6
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:7
msgid ""
"Fast snapshot load is an extension of the postcopy migration feature to disk "
"loads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:10
msgid ""
"Unlike a usual snapshot load, which requires all VM data (RAM as well as "
"device states) to be loaded into host RAM from the snapshot file for the "
"guest to run, fast snapshot load uses postcopy infrastructure to load in "
"only the required device states and allows RAM pages to be loaded after the "
"guest starts execution. The idea is to start the guest and serve its page "
"faults on the go, reducing the perceived resume time for large snapshots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:19
msgid "Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:20
msgid ""
"This feature combines postcopy migration and mapped-ram capabilities to load "
"RAM pages on demand. It is done by catching guest faults using Linux "
"``userfaultfd`` and loading the page by calculating the offset of its "
"location in the snapshot file using mapped-ram capabilities."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:26
msgid "Fault Thread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:27
msgid ""
"The fault thread uses Linux ``userfaultfd`` to catch page faults caused by "
"guest and directly load the page from the snapshot file. It is very similar "
"to network postcopy fault thread, with primary difference being it loads "
"pages directly by reading from the snapshot file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:33
msgid "Eager Thread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:34
msgid ""
"Eager thread iterates over all pages in RAM and loads each page not yet "
"loaded by fault thread. It is required as unlike network postcopy where "
"majority of RAM has already been loaded via precopy, here entire RAM is "
"waiting to be loaded. If there is no eager loading thread each page will "
"only be loaded when it is required by guest. In case there are some "
"background pages that are never/rarely accessed by guest, the system will be "
"locked in migration state indefinitely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:43
msgid "Synchronization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:44
msgid ""
"In order to make sure both of these threads do not load the same page twice "
"potentially overwriting and corrupting user RAM, a bitmap is used "
"(``RAMBlock->pending_bmap``) which tracks the pages claimed to be loaded by "
"threads. This prevents race condition when one thread is loading the page "
"and other one tries to do the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:51
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:53
msgid ""
"Simply enable ``mapped-ram`` and ``postcopy-ram`` capabilities on the "
"destination:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:56
msgid ""
"migrate_set_capability mapped-ram on\n"
"migrate_set_capability postcopy-ram on"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:61
msgid "Use a ``file:`` URI for migration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:63
msgid "migrate_incoming file:/path/to/snapshot/file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:68
msgid "Limitations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:70
msgid "Multifd"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:71
msgid ""
"Fast snapshot load is currently incompatible with ``multifd`` capability. "
"While ``mapped-ram`` allows for parallel disk I/O, coupling it with "
"``postcopy`` capability requires additional infrastructure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:76
msgid "Host OS support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:77
msgid ""
"Because this feautre essentially depends on ``userfaultfd`` to trap page "
"faults, it is supported only on Linux hosts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:80
msgid "vhost-user"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../devel/migration/fast-snapshot-load.rst:81
msgid "Fast snapshot load does not currently support ``vhost-user`` backends."
msgstr ""
